# Two settlers meet head-on and pass (docs/rules/settlers.md, "Passing"). Taking the second road down sends its carrier
# home west along the first road; the woodcutter of a hut put down at 13,10 walks out east along it. The carrier waits on
# the node the woodcutter holds, and the woodcutter steps east past it: each takes the other's node.
# Run it on the layout: sh tools/play-run.sh head-on-pass --layout layouts/head-on-pass.jsonc --fps 10
wait 32
name cr 16 11 carrier
button Remove
click-tile 15 11
button Remove
wait 1
button Woodcutter
click-tile 13 10
button Woodcutter
wait 1
name wc 10 10 woodcutter
shot start
wait 16
# Tick 496: the carrier, heading west, is blocked on 13,11 and waits.
expect cr.x@496 = 13
expect cr.heading@496 = -3
expect cr.frame@496 = 0x54
expect cr.timer@496 = 0x7f
# Tick 499: the woodcutter steps east past it. The carrier takes 12,11 with the shape and time of its step back west.
expect wc.x@499 = 13
expect wc.y@499 = 11
expect wc.heading@499 = 3
expect cr.x@499 = 12
expect cr.y@499 = 11
expect cr.heading@499 = 0
expect cr.frame@499 = 31
expect cr.timer@499 = 255
expect-event cr stepped cause razed
events wc woodcutter
events cr carrier
shot passed 13 11 2 2
